      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "For any quadrilateral with the property that the extensions of the opposite sides meet at a point (inclusive), the base angles are equal in measure.  Therefore, triangle $BCE$ is isosceles, and thus $\\angle ECB = \\angle EBC$.  Likewise, triangle $ACE$ is isosceles and $\\angle ACE = \\angle AEC$.  By equal angles, triangles $ACE$ and $BCD$ are similar.  Therefore, in triangle $ACE$, $\\angle BAC = \\angle EDC = 43^\\circ$ by AA similarity, for a total of $180^\\circ - 43^\\circ - 43^\\circ - 43^\\circ = 92^\\circ$, and hence $\\angle CED = \\boxed{92^\\circ}$. The answer is 92",
