      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "First, we can notice that vertical angles created by respective tangents will have the same value. Hence, we know that,\n\n\n\\[\\angle{BCA}=\\angle{ECD}\\]\n\nSince $\\angle{BAE}=43^\\circ$, we can combine the angles from $\\angle{BCA}+\\angle{BAC}$ in order to get $\\angle{ECD}$, which can be mathematically shown as,\n\n\\[\\angle{ECD}=43^\\circ\\]\n\nWe then notice that,\n\n\n\\[\\angle{CED}=\\angle{ECD}+\\angle{DCE}=43^\\circ+90^\\circ-75^\\circ=98^\\circ\\]\n\nTherefore, $\\angle{CED}=\\boxed{98}$ degrees. The answer is 98",
